message: "If you use these materials in your teaching or research, please cite them as below."
title: "LS100: Computational Behavioral Sciences — Foundations of Data Science and Applied AI/ML for Conducting Research in Behavioral Sciences"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Souvik
    family-names: Mandal
    affiliation: "Harvard University"
abstract: >-
  Open course materials for LS100 (Harvard University): a research-based course on
  quantifying human and animal behavior using Python, data science, computer vision,
  audio analysis, and applied AI/ML. Includes Jupyter notebooks (from Python
  fundamentals through pose estimation, audio feature extraction, and statistics)
  and written reading guides.
